410
00:30:23,364 --> 00:30:48,962
[SPEAKER_06]: So, that's why in that other talk we did, basically, if you train your mind towards the ultimate uncertainty, so you stop resisting it, trying to get rid of it, trying to antidote it, trying to... or act out of it, welcome it, delight in it, to... towards distraction from it and so on, that uncertainty that you will train your mind in regard to, to become dispassionate and not averse towards or afraid from, is nibbāna, the ultimate uncertainty.

411
00:30:49,363 --> 00:30:49,703
[SPEAKER_06]: That's it.

412
00:30:49,783 --> 00:30:51,224
[SPEAKER_06]: That's the phenomenon of nibbāna.

413
00:30:52,740 --> 00:30:53,301
[SPEAKER_06]: Here and now.

414
00:30:57,405 --> 00:31:08,717
